    rdf:value """May 7. 1895. Tuesday - Villa Rosa. Fiesole.
Poets are people who go straight from feeling to expression, not via thought.
One’s results are, after all, only moments in one’s thoughts. 
May 10. Friday 1895 
I have not written - I have just been struggling to live - that is to keep happy and feel a springing up of vitality - so necessary to “living” in any satisfactory sense - I had a rather knock-down blow, although it ought not to have been unexpected, in realizing that the children must be inevitably trained as Catholics. I had planned before just what I could do and could not, and saw no reason to change my mind. But """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 124 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1894-95> .

